 node3 (RHEL7) so TCP traffic to node4:8080 is steered across the first transit network (node1 eth1 10.10.1.0/30 ↔ node2 vtnet1) and TCP traffic to node4:9090 across the second transit network (node1 eth2 10.10.2.0/30 ↔ node2 vtnet2), with both flows successfully reaching node4 over the shared 10.100.106.0/24 network as the final hop. Implementation: iptables mangle marks + policy ip rules/routes on node3 (RHEL7, persisted via firewalld direct rules + NetworkManager dispatcher script), VyOS policy-route ruleset with two static routing tables on node1, and OPNsense opt1/opt2 interfaces + pf pass rules on node2. All four nodes were restarted one at a time (native reboot mechanisms), boot-identity change was proven for each (boot_id for Linux nodes, kern.boottime for FreeBSD/OPNsense), and post-restart the full configuration, routing, firewall rules, and end-to-end port-8080/port-9090 flows over their respective distinct transit networks were reverified via tcpdump captures on node1's and node2's transit interfaces.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed all 4 nodes: node1=VyOS router, node2=OPNsense (FreeBSD) router, node3/node4=RHEL7 endpoints, all sharing 10.100.106.0/24\",\"Discovered node1 eth1/eth2 and node2 vtnet1/vtnet2 are two independent unconfigured transit links between node1 and node2 (verified via ARP/ping pairing test)\",\"Configured node1 (VyOS): eth1=10.10.1.1/30 (transit-net-1), eth2=10.10.2.1/30 (transit-net-2), policy route ruleset PBR-NODE4 matching dest 10.100.106.13 tcp/8080->table 101 (via transit-net-1) and tcp/9090->table 102 (via transit-net-2), committed and saved\",\"Configured node2 (OPNsense): added opt1 (vtnet1, 10.10.1.2/30) and opt2 (vtnet2, 10.10.2.2/30) interfaces via config.xml edit + configctl interface reconfigure, added pf pass rules for tcp/8080 on opt1 and tcp/9090 on opt2 destined to node4\",\"Configured node3 (RHEL7): iptables mangle OUTPUT marks by destination port, ip rule/ip route policy tables 101/102 routing node4's /32 via node1 as next-hop; persisted via firewalld --direct rules and a NetworkManager dispatcher script\",\"Opened firewalld ports 8080/9090 on node4 and started Python HTTP listeners for testing\",\"Verified via tcpdump on node1 eth1/eth2 and node2 vtnet1/vtnet2 that port 8080 traffic used only transit-net-1 and port 9090 traffic used only transit-net-2, with successful HTTP 200 responses from node4\",\"Captured healthy baseline (boot markers + config/service state) on all 4 nodes\",\"Restarted node4, node3, node2, node1 one at a time using native reboot mechanisms, polled each until exec access returned, and proved changed boot identity (boot_id/kern.boottime) for each\",\"Restored node4's HTTP listeners after its reboot (firewalld ports persisted natively; listeners were ephemeral test processes)\",\"Verified full recovery after each restart: VyOS policy routes/interfaces persisted via saved config.boot, OPNsense interfaces/pf rules persisted via config.xml, RHEL7 node3 routing recovered via NetworkManager dispatcher script\",\"Ran final end-to-end verification after all 4 restarts confirming both flows still traverse their correct distinct transit networks and reach node4 successfully\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Two independent transit networks exist between node1 and node2\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a8a7df1751364cd7\",\"cmd-d4d6d700c6d34294\",\"cmd-1d5727bf1fce4400\",\"cmd-df7fc109816f4895\",\"cmd-0f753408d5bb44d2\"],\"summary\":\"eth1(node1)<->vtnet1(node2)=10.10.1.0/30 and eth2(node1)<->vtnet2(node2)=10.10.2.0/30 confirmed as the two distinct L2 transit links via ARP pairing test\"},{\"requirement\":\"Port 8080 traffic from node3 to node4 steered across the first transit network\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9979e025a3f141c5\",\"cmd-e099da26c3324508\",\"cmd-eb2199b17daf4bf1\",\"cmd-888c9826e0e24443\"],\"summary\":\"tcpdump on node1 eth1 and node2 vtnet1 captured the full TCP handshake/GET/FIN for 10.100.106.12->10.100.106.13:8080, confirming exclusive use of transit-net-1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Port 9090 traffic from node3 to node4 steered across the second transit network\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9979e025a3f141c5\",\"cmd-e099da26c3324508\",\"cmd-eb2199b17daf4bf1\",\"cmd-888c9826e0e24443\"],\"summary\":\"Same capture window shows the 9090 flow appearing only on eth2/vtnet2 (transit-net-2), not on eth1/vtnet1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Both flows reach node4 successfully\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e099da26c3324508\",\"cmd-084b9bca30434a0e\"],\"summary\":\"curl from node3 to node4:8080 and :9090 both returned HTTP 200 both before and after the full restart cycle\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 (VyOS) healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d945969ac8324b5c\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 2eb8b6e8... plus interface addresses and PBR routing tables 101/102 as healthy baseline\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-943a398a4465468a\",\"cmd-e97c35604cb04049\",\"cmd-b2d501f6ca454708\",\"cmd-c49c9da2b1714f35\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged and connection lost; polling timed out then succeeded with boot_id cfdf5c8f... (changed from baseline); post-restart interfaces, PBR tables, and ip_forward all recovered from saved VyOS config\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 (OPNsense) healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2fabb641f47c44c6\"],\"summary\":\"Captured kern.boottime 05:37:41 plus vtnet1/vtnet2 addresses and pf pass rules for 8080/9090 as healthy baseline\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-959fdea7b86a4b0a\",\"cmd-0b22e5906f2342af\",\"cmd-5988f0258bd34d77\",\"cmd-cf48af14557f4b97\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command dropped the SSH connection; polling timed out then returned new kern.boottime 05:50:10 (changed from baseline); post-restart vtnet1/vtnet2 addresses, pf rules, and routes all recovered from config.xml\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 